\par
\b 1. Purpose\b0\par
SMC is a self-hosted marketing dashboard. The Google Ads integration provides OAuth connect and read-only analytics for account and campaign metrics (impressions, clicks, cost, conversions, CTR) inside the SMC UI.\par
\par
\b 2. Users\b0\par
Internal HawkBytes team (employees) during development and client reporting. External end-customers may be added later after Standard access if needed; this Basic Access application is for internal use first.\par
\par
\b 3. Architecture (high level)\b0\par
- Frontend: React dashboard at /google-ads and Dashboard Google Ads panel\par
- Backend: Node/Express API under /api/v1/google-ads/*\par
- Auth: OAuth 2.0 (Google) with scope https://www.googleapis.com/auth/adwords\par
- Storage: Encrypted refresh tokens; cached daily account/campaign metrics in PostgreSQL\par
- API usage: ListAccessibleCustomers + GoogleAdsService.Search (GAQL) for metrics\par
\par
\b 4. Google Ads API capabilities used\b0\par
- Account Management (link accessible customers)\par
- Reporting (read-only metrics sync)\par
No campaign creation, bidding changes, or keyword mutation in the initial release.\par
\par
\b 5. OAuth / security\b0\par
- Web application OAuth client in Google Cloud\par
- Redirect URI points to SMC backend callback\par
- Developer token from Google Ads Manager (MCC) API Center\par
- Tokens encrypted at rest; access limited to authenticated SMC users on Medium/Premium plans\par
\par
\b 6. Data flow\b0\par
1. User clicks Connect Google Ads in SMC\par
2. Google OAuth consent\par
3. Backend stores linked customer ID + encrypted tokens\par
4. Sync pulls date-range metrics via API and stores them for charts/tables\par
\par
